cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use allograph-attacks, please cite this release. The code is licensed
  MIT; the run logs in runs/ and the builder table in docs/ are licensed CC BY 4.0.
type: software
title: "allograph-attacks: testbed, run logs and builder table for allograph attacks on shared agent platforms"
abstract: >-
  A synthetic shared agent platform, an experiment harness, the logs of every
  reported run and the table from a review of eight shared agent
  builders. An allograph attack is a line that a co-author adds to a shared
  agent workflow and that runs with the permissions of whoever starts the
  workflow. The artifact accompanies the paper "Your Keys, Their Words:
  Allograph Attacks on Shared Agent Platforms".
